    and M6 additionally cannot go below Newton, which is why the two NGC 1052 galaxies and Pal 4 are blank there too.
  M0: 33/35 rows reachable; required a_1/a_0 spans 3.089e-02 to 2.051e+03 = a factor 66393, log-spread 0.956 dex
  M1: 26/35 rows reachable; required a_1/a_0 spans 7.389e-02 to 2.227e+00 = a factor 30, log-spread 0.413 dex
  M2: 26/35 rows reachable; required a_1/a_0 spans 1.695e-02 to 3.308e+00 = a factor 195, log-spread 0.683 dex
  M6:  7/35 rows reachable; required a_1/a_0 spans 4.319e-03 to 2.294e+00 = a factor 531, log-spread 1.010 dex
  [PASS] 2a (can fail; a single further scale would PASS it) THE ROWS DO NOT AGREE ON a_1. Solved one at a time, the additive-floor scale spans a factor of order 100 and the nested-kernel scale a factor of order 1000. A scale measured to a factor of 100 is not a constant of nature; the ledger is not asking for one more number   (M1 a_1/a_0 = 7.389e-02 .. 2.227e+00 (x30, 0.413 dex); M2 = 1.695e-02 .. 3.308e+00 (x195, 0.683 dex))

  WHY they disagree, measured: d log R_required / d log y over all 35 amplitude rows = -0.147; over the 15 cluster/group rows alone = +0.058.
  A second scale is a TRANSITION, so it has a characteristic slope. Tuned to pass through the clusters' own median point (y = 0.113, R = 2.24), M1 predicts d log R/d log y = -0.139 and M2 predicts -0.159.
  2b RESTATED with a bar taken from the data instead of invented: across the cluster front's own 2.28 decades of acceleration, M1 tuned to its median point predicts the boost to CHANGE by -0.318 dex; it is measured to change by +0.133 dex. The disagreement is 0.451 dex against the front's entire measured scatter of 0.114 dex.
  [PASS] 2b (can fail) the ledger's required boost runs the WRONG WAY. Every second-scale mechanism must make the boost DECLINE as acceleration rises -- that is what 'switching on deeper down' means -- and across the cluster front the boost is measured to RISE. The sign of the trend is opposite, and the size of the disagreement exceeds the entire scatter of the front it is trying to explain   (mechanism -0.318 dex across the front vs measured +0.133 dex; disagreement 0.451 dex against the front's own scatter 0.114 dex (measured slope +0.058, M1 -0.139, M2 -0.159))

