6.  MUTATION CONTROLS, and the LambdaCDM/Newtonian alternative computed beside
==============================================================================================================================
  [PASS] MUT-1 (must PASS; if it failed the keeper suite would be broken rather than the mechanism) with a_1 driven to 1e-9 a_0 every mechanism collapses to the unmodified framework and every keeper must pass, reproducing the baselines   (K1 0.1327 (baseline 0.1327); all 7 keepers pass)
  [PASS] MUT-2 (must FAIL; this is the control proving the keepers have teeth) with a_1 = 3 a_0 -- a floor three times the acceleration scale itself -- the keepers must break loudly. If they did not, they would be incapable of excluding anything   (broken: K1/K2/K3/K4/K5/K6/K7; RAR rms 0.364 dex, deep-tail a_0 off by 1.25 dex, outer v slope +0.463 vs observed +0.047)
  [PASS] MUT-3 (must FAIL, and it does) the standard a_0 mutation: divide a_0 by 1000 and the framework becomes Newton exactly -- the RAR keeper's residual reproduces the Newtonian one to better than 0.002 dex in both the mean and the scatter, and the zero point moves to +0.43 dex, eight times the keeper's own 0.05 dex bar. The keeper is measuring the kernel   (a_0/1000: mean +0.4295, rms 0.2803; Newton on the same points: mean +0.4298, rms 0.2809; unmodified framework +0.0338 / 0.1327)

  THE ALTERNATIVE, COUNTED HONESTLY. LambdaCDM fits every one of these 35 systems, both signs included, with a per-system halo: 70 free parameters (two per system) plus a stellar M/L each. It does so because it has one free function per object, which is exactly the freedom this angle was trying to avoid buying.
  A second acceleration scale buys ONE parameter (or two for M3/M4/M7). The finding here is not that one parameter is too few to fit 35 numbers -- it is that the ONE parameter cannot fit even the 15-row homogeneous cluster block, because it has the wrong SHAPE, and that any value of it large enough to matter destroys the rotation-curve results the framework already has.
  Newton on the same SPARC points with no modification at all: vertical residual mean +0.430 dex, rms 0.281 dex, against the framework's +0.034 / 0.133. The keepers are real successes and that is why breaking them costs something.

