  THE ONE POSITIVE FINDING, and it is worth as much as the negatives. Restricted to the fifteen cluster and group
  rows -- one sign, EFE-free, four decades of mass -- there IS a one-parameter description that works:
      a CONSTANT boost of x2.30 in acceleration           -> rms 0.114 dex, 8/15 rows inside 0.10 dex
      equivalently a_0 larger by x6.63 for these systems -> rms 0.127 dex, 8/15 rows inside 0.10 dex
  Both are the SAME statement (a constant deep-MOND boost eta in acceleration IS a_0 -> eta^2 a_0), and BOTH fits
  drove the transition scale to the edge of the grid -- M3's a_1 went to 1e-4 a_0 and M4's step swallowed the whole
  sample. That is the ledger telling us, through the fit rather than through an argument, that it wants a CONSTANT
  and not a TRANSITION. A constant is not a second scale. It is the first one, broken.
  And it is not available: that same constant moves the RAR zero point to -0.327 dex against a 0.05 bar and the deep-tail a_0 by 0.891 dex against a 0.10 bar.

  'rows fixed' counts liabilities brought inside 0.10 dex. For reference, the UNMODIFIED framework already has 6/35 rows inside 0.10 dex, so any mechanism scoring at or below that number has bought nothing at all.

  AND, AGAINST THE NEGATIVE VERDICT, what the mechanisms DO buy, reported before it is dismissed: the best of them move 10 rows inside 0.10 dex against the unmodified framework's 6, i.e. three or four extra rows out of 35. That is a real if small gain and it is not nothing.
  What it is not is a unification. The residual over the whole ledger goes from 0.551 dex unmodified to 0.424 dex at best -- a gain of 0.127 dex for one new constant of nature, still 4.2x the 0.10 dex bar the hunt sets for a Kepler-grade relation, and paid for with two to five keepers.
  [PASS] 7a (can fail; the bar is the item's own 0.10 dex, taken from the hunt's definition of a Kepler-grade relation and not adjustable here) THE HEADLINE. A second acceleration scale does not unify the ledger. Fitted to all 35 amplitude rows, the best mechanism of any kind -- one or two free parameters, seven functional forms tried -- leaves a residual of 0.42 dex, four times that bar. AGAINST THE VERDICT AND REPORTED FIRST: it is not zero gain. The residual does fall from 0.55 to 0.42 dex and three to four extra rows come inside 0.10 dex. That gain is real, it is small, and every mechanism delivering it breaks two to five of the seven galactic successes   (unmodified ledger residual 0.551 dex, 6/35 rows within 0.10; best mechanism residual 0.424 dex (M0 0.511/10, M1 0.473/9, M2 0.470/6, M3 0.516/9, M4 0.424/6, M6 0.551/6, M7 0.495/7))

